  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Mavenclad (cladribine), a purine antimetabolite. Version: 1; Original: 7/05/2019; Approval: 9/20/2019; Effective: 11/20/2019.",
    "Encoded: approval criteria 1-6 and denial criteria 1-5. Closed RRMS and active SPMS indications exclude clinically isolated syndrome. Baseline labs, counseling and prior therapy are attestations. Counseling is not applicable only for patients not of reproductive potential.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): up to 10 tablets per cycle. No numeric quantity enforcement.",
    "Cautions (notes only): increased malignancy risk; fetal harm if administered during pregnancy; reduced immune defense increases infection risk. Immunizations should be administered at least 4-6 weeks before initiating treatment.",
    "PDL status unknown: PDF is silent. MS peer alternatives require separate eligibility evaluation.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, authorization duration, reauthorization, dosing, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
